<!--
  modules/history_browser/pom.xml — Stage 2-f Task 4 module POM (Wave D)
  (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-stage2f-remaining-modules.md).

  STATUS: ADDITIVE and RUN BY HAND (mvn -pl modules/history_browser -am
  package from the reactor root, or mvn -f modules/history_browser/pom.xml
  package). Ant (modules/history_browser/build.xml + build.incl.xml) remains
  the real build; nothing here is wired into CMake or any release build yet.

  WHY THIS MODULE. Part of Wave D — four modules whose only unmigrated-wave
  dependency was gui (Wave C, now in the reactor). history_browser is the
  command-history window (CommandHistory.java's Swing JList/tree UI) plus its
  toolbar/context-menu actions (14 files, five in the top-level package, nine
  under actions/).

  STEP 1 FINDINGS (./maven-module-deps.sh history_browser, 14 files):
    [1] imports (excluding the module's own packages): org.scilab.modules.
        commons{,.gui}, graphic_objects.graphicObject, gui.* (bridge.
        {contextmenu,menuitem,tab,toolbar,window}, console, contextmenu,
        events.callback, menu, menubar, menuitem, messagebox, tab,
        tabfactory, textbox, toolbar, utils, window), history_manager,
        localization — five reactor dependencies, all below (all already
        migrated: Wave C for gui, earlier waves for the rest). No vendored
        third-party import anywhere in this module.
    [2] reflection targets — THE TOOL ITSELF MISSED ONE HERE, FOUND BY A
        MANUAL SWEEP (see the highlighted paragraph below): the script
        reported "(none)", but actions/EditInScinotesAction.java genuinely
        reaches org.scilab.modules.scinotes.SciNotes via Class.forName at
        runtime — RULED OUT below for the same reason every other module's
        scinotes/core.Scilab reflection finding has been (scinotes is Wave E,
        nowhere near migrated; a compile-time dependency here would likely
        cycle, which is exactly why the source uses reflection to begin
        with — EditInScinotesAction.java's own comment says so explicitly).
    [3] fully-qualified uses with no import: every org.scilab.modules.
        {commons,graphic_objects,gui,history_manager,localization}.* name in
        this category is already covered by the five reactor dependencies
        above (SwingScilabContextMenu, SwingScilabMenuItem,
        SwingScilabDockablePanel, SwingScilabToolBar, SwingScilabWindow,
        ScilabConsole, ContextMenu, ScilabContextMenu, CallBack,
        CommonCallBack, Menu, ScilabMenu, MenuBar, ScilabMenuBar, MenuItem,
        ScilabMenuItem, MessageBox, ScilabMessageBox, SimpleTab,
        AbstractScilabTabFactory, ScilabTabFactory, ScilabTextBox, TextBox,
        ScilabToolBar, ToolBar, ClosingOperationsManager,
        WindowsConfigurationManager, ScilabWindow, HistoryManagement,
        Messages, ScilabGeneralPrefs, FindIconHelper, ScilabGUIUtilities,
        ScilabKeyStroke, ScilabLAF, CallBack (graphic_objects.graphicObject)),
        nothing new. org.scilab.modules.scinotes.SciNotes is NOT in this
        list either — see the paragraph below for why, and why that absence
        does not mean the finding was safe to skip.

  A REAL GAP IN maven-module-deps.sh, FOUND BY THIS MODULE, NOT DOCUMENTED IN
  THE SCRIPT'S OWN HEADER. EditInScinotesAction.java:37 declares `private
  static final String SCINOTES_PACKAGE = "org.scilab.modules.scinotes.
  SciNotes";` and then calls `Class.forName(SCINOTES_PACKAGE)` at lines 57
  and 98 — a genuine reflective load of an unmigrated module's class, exactly
  the shape [2] exists to catch. It caught NEITHER this call NOR the literal
  as a [3] fully-qualified use, for two compounding reasons, confirmed by
  reading the script (not guessed):
    - [2]'s own regex, `(Class\.forName|loadClass)\(\s*"[^"]+"`, requires the
      double-quoted string literal DIRECTLY inside the call's parentheses.
      Here the call site passes a variable (SCINOTES_PACKAGE), not an inline
      literal, so the call itself never matches — contrast modules/ui_data/
      pom.xml's OpenFileInSciNotesAction.java, which DOES call
      `Class.forName("org.scilab.modules.scinotes.SciNotes")` inline and WAS
      correctly caught by this same regex.
    - [3]'s regex requires the fully-qualified name to be preceded by `@` or
      a character OUTSIDE the class `[A-Za-z0-9_."]` — and that negated class
      itself EXCLUDES the double-quote character, so a name occurring as the
      very first token inside a string literal (immediately after the
      opening `"`, e.g. the SCINOTES_PACKAGE constant's own initializer) has
      a `"` as its preceding character and structurally cannot match. The
      same is true of ConsoleTabFactory.java-style self-referential `CLASS =
      "org.scilab.modules...ClassName"` constants seen in this wave (core,
      history_browser, ui_data each have one) — [3] is silent on all of them,
      by the same mechanism, though those particular ones are harmless
      (self-references to the declaring module's own class).
  CONSEQUENCE: a module can hide a real reflective dependency on an
  unmigrated module behind one level of constant indirection and this tool
  will report a clean "(none)" for [2] and say nothing in [3] either — the
  worst kind of miss, a false-negative silence rather than the
  over-reporting [3] already warns about. Found here only because Task 4's
  own verification step ran an independent `grep -rn 'Class\.forName\|
  loadClass('` sweep across all four modules before trusting the tool's
  "(none)". RULED OUT exactly as intended once found — no compile-time
  dependency added — but the absence in the tool's own output was NOT
  evidence of absence in the source, and should not be treated as such by
  whichever module hits this shape next. Not fixed here (the script itself
  is out of scope for a module-POM task), but flagged loudly per this
  campaign's evidence-before-assertion standard.
  No manifest.class-path anywhere in build.xml (confirmed again in the
  Ant-built jar's manifest: Class-Path is the literal, never-interpolated
  string "${manifest.class-path}").

  IMPLEMENTATION-VERSION: present, frozen at the literal "00000000 0000",
  positioned between Implementation-Title and Implementation-Vendor exactly
  where Ant's own jar places it (confirmed against modules/history_browser/
  jar/org.scilab.modules.history_browser.jar's actual manifest before
  extraction: live value there was "20260719 1729", a DSTAMP/TSTAMP pair).
  Vendor string double-encoded ("Ã¨", bytes c3 83 c2 a8) — extracted, never
  retyped, same as every other module.
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <parent>
    <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
    <artifactId>scilab-modules-parent</artifactId>
    <version>2027.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    <relativePath>../../pom.xml</relativePath>
  </parent>

  <artifactId>history_browser</artifactId>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>

  <!-- build.xml:19 <property name="library.title" value="Scilab history browser"/> -->
  <name>Scilab history browser</name>

  <dependencies>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.commons.{ScilabGeneralPrefs, gui.FindIconHelper,
         gui.ScilabGUIUtilities, gui.ScilabKeyStroke, gui.ScilabLAF}. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>commons</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.graphic_objects.graphicObject.CallBack. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>graphic_objects</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.gui.* — the widest package family here (bridge.
         {contextmenu,menuitem,tab,toolbar,window}, console, contextmenu,
         events.callback, menu, menubar, menuitem, messagebox, tab,
         tabfactory, textbox, toolbar, utils, window). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>gui</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.history_manager.HistoryManagement. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>history_manager</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.localization.Messages — the ordinary
         reactor-sibling idiom used across nearly every module. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>localization</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <!-- build.incl.xml:22 <property name="src.dir" location="src/java/"/>.
         Same source tree Ant compiles — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
         identical comment; nothing module-specific to add here. -->
    <sourceDirectory>src/java</sourceDirectory>

    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-jar-plugin</artifactId>
        <configuration>
          <archive>
            <!-- addMavenDescriptor=false and the Built-By entry are
                 inherited from the parent POM — not redeclared here. Same
                 manifestFile mechanism as modules/localization/pom.xml (see
                 that file's build comment for the full rationale).
                 MANIFEST-section.MF's bytes were EXTRACTED from the actual
                 Ant-built jar's META-INF/MANIFEST.MF (unzip -p
                 modules/history_browser/jar/org.scilab.modules.
                 history_browser.jar META-INF/MANIFEST.MF), never retyped:
                 Specification-Vendor and Implementation-Vendor both carry
                 the double-mangled "Ã¨" (bytes c3 83 c2 a8) — see
                 modules/localization/pom.xml's fuller comment for the
                 mechanism. Implementation-Version is present, frozen at the
                 literal "00000000 0000", positioned between
                 Implementation-Title and Implementation-Vendor exactly
                 where Ant places it. -->
            <manifestFile>${project.basedir}/src/main/manifest/MANIFEST-section.MF</manifestFile>
          </archive>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
